course: dictionary
lesson: 7462
title: Population: how many live here
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A population is the number of people who live in a place. It can also mean all the animals or plants of one kind living in one area, such as the bee population.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Many wild animal populations have fallen since 1970» tells you that animals are counted too, and fallen means the number went down.
explain: «The Chinese water deer is threatened in China, but escaped water deer spread in England, which now holds a big share of the world's population.» Ask: what word would fit here? Try "number of deer living in a place". That fits, so population means the number of animals of one kind.
fact: Population means the number of people, or animals or plants of one kind, living in an area.
fact: A large population means that many people or animals live in one place.
fact: Population growth means the number gets bigger over time.
fact: In maths, population can also mean the whole group you are studying in statistics.
fact: Populations of towns and countries are often compared, rounded, added and put in order in geography lessons.
exercise: «Many wild animal populations have fallen since 1970.» What does population mean in this sentence? | A map of an animal's home | *The number of animals of one kind living in an area | A type of bird that sings | The food that animals eat
exercise: Ella says the population of her town is the number of shops there. What does population mean? | The name of the town | The number of shops in town | *The number of people who live there | The roads that go into town
exercise: Which phrase means a place with many people living in it? | A sharp border | *A large population | Trade goods | A vague stretch of forest
test: «The world's population» means | *All the people living in the world | A map of the world | A holiday around the world | The biggest country in the world
test: Population growth means | Shrinking | Fewer buildings in a town | *The number of people or animals getting bigger over time | Tall plants in a garden
exam: Which word in «Many wild animal populations have fallen since 1970» tells you the number went down? | *fallen | population | since | wild
